From 4612d4dfedd474b50606c905ea87b85bcbb2dc6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-D <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:36:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] 0950 redfin: ADSP FastRPC channel, /dev/redwood-fastrpc,
 SMMU identity

sweet_adsp.c answers the DSP's fastrpcglink-apps-dsp (64 intents of 0x64
bytes, as the DT) and glink_ssr channels. /dev/redwood-fastrpc (one opener,
0600) carries 40-byte FastRPC messages to the DSP (write; ENOTCONN before
the DSP has opened the channel) and its answers back (read; blocking unless
O_NONBLOCK; ECONNRESET once the DSP has given up). ioctl FASTRPC_SMMU_IDENTITY
gives stream 0x1403-0x1405 a context bank of the apps SMMU with translation
off (the 0921 / radio.c way, logged with SMR/S2CR/CBAR/SCTLR); messages whose
session (addr >> 32) has no stream set up are refused. ioctl FASTRPC_ALLOC
(addition to the plan's ABI): contiguous RAM below 4 GiB from the GPU pool
(sweet_gpu_pool_alloc, as the camera's frames: XNU's RAM starts at 4 GiB
here), zeroed through a device mapping, kept for the DSP (32 buffers, reused
at the same size); the range handed out is logged. Boot-arg adsp=2: the DSP
is started when /dev/redwood-fastrpc is first opened (fastrpcd is up before
the sensors PD asks for its files), adsp=1 as before; adsp_fastrpc=0: the
old way; =2: every message logged. adsp_sleep=1: our SMP2P item
also carries Android's other APPS entries, "sleepstate" = 1 (APPS awake)
and "rdbg" = 0. adsp_qlog=1: IPCRTR datagrams and intent events logged
(SWEET QLOG:, first 200 lines, then one line per 100 datagrams). Poke f 0/1/2/3/5: status, the DSP's words
and last words, QRTR services, SMMU identity, SMMU faults.
